# OS-aware script launcher

`run.sh` reads the existing adjacent `.man` contracts under `bin`, `dev`, and
`sys`; it does not maintain a second script list. It detects Linux, macOS, or
Windows internally, hides incompatible and non-launchable commands, and never
uses `eval`.

The launcher needs Python 3. Commands whose shebang declares `uv` also need
`uv`, so their inline dependency contracts remain isolated and reproducible.

## Usage

```sh
./run.sh list
./run.sh security-audit audit --scope system
./run.sh disk health
./run.sh clean
```

Use a listed short name or its repository-relative path. Remaining arguments
are passed unchanged to that command. Ambiguous names, traversal, malformed
help metadata, symlinks, unsupported platforms, and incompatible scripts are
rejected.

`./run.sh --self-test` validates all three operating-system catalogs without
running their commands.
